# bandwidth.cyr — memory bandwidth enrichment post-pass
#
# The detectors set memory bandwidth themselves: CUDA from nvidia-smi's
# memory clock and the bus width (parse_cuda_output), ROCm from the card's
# pp_dpm_mclk and its KFD node (detect_rocm_at, 2.5.5). Through 2.5.4 this
# pass computed the ROCm figure from "/sys/class/drm/card<device_id>", a card
# the profile's ordinal does not name, and from the pp_dpm_mclk level index
# instead of the clock, so it was never right.

# Enrich profiles with memory bandwidth. The registry's post-passes and the
# library bundle call it; every backend that can report a bandwidth now sets
# it at detection, so there is nothing left to fill.
fn enrich_bandwidth(profiles) {
    return 0;
}
